  "stage": {
    "routeId": "camino-norte",
    "index": 5,
    "count": 34,
    "name": "Gernika to Lezama",
    "theme": "The approach",
    "narrative": "A shorter day, by Norte standards. You climb Bizkargi through mixed forest, pass hamlets too small to appear on maps, and by early afternoon you are in Lezama, a suburban village with a pilgrim albergue, a bar, and a church. The rhythm of the past three inland days — climb, forest, village, descent, village — is about to be broken by the arrival in Bilbao tomorrow. Use the quiet of Lezama.",
    "closing": "Four days into an inland section. What is the forest teaching that the coast could not?",
